   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Three groups",
     "texto": [
      "**Oxytone** (stress on the last syllable: **café**, **avó**, **também**). **Paroxytone** (stress on the second-to-last syllable: **casa**, **fácil**). **Proparoxytone** (stress on the third-to-last syllable: **lâmpada**, **pássaro**). **Lisboa** is paroxytone: Lis-**bo**-a."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Common rules",
     "texto": [
      "Many oxytone words ending in **-a(s), -e(s), -o(s), -em, -ens** take a written accent: **sofá, café, avó, também, parabéns**. All proparoxytones take an accent. Many paroxytones take one when they end in consonants such as **-l, -n, -r, -x**: **fácil, hífen, caráter, carácter, tórax**. The AO90 accepts the variants **caráter** and **carácter**; the plural can be **carateres** or **caracteres**. There are more endings and exceptions: check a dictionary when in doubt."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
